> Christian is right that, for a CFA model, the correlations and their delta method CIs and p-values are already in the output of standardizedSolution.
>
> Assuming that the model is not a CFA model, then whether it is easy to define the correlations using ":=" depends on the form of the model. Given that lavInspect() with "cor.lv <http://cor.lv>" has been used, bootstrapLavaan() in lavaan (a very useful function) maybe the most straightforward solution:
>
> library(lavaan)
> #> This is lavaan 0.6-15
> #> lavaan is FREE software! Please report any bugs.
> # Create a dataset from a simple mediation model
