> The p-value obtained when comparing the two models (lavTestLRT(fit_cstr, fit)) is the same as the p-value of the difference in the slopes ?

You mean the Wald z test for a difference parameter in the summary() output?  No, but they would be asymptotically equivalent tests of the same H0.  Did you define a difference parameter?

s ~ c(a1, a2)*1
a_diff := a1 - a2

> I was fitting this model with DLD1 as a predictor of the intercept and the slope as below.

Assuming DLD1 is a dummy code, the group difference is the effect of DLD1 on the growth factor.

> I would very much appreciate your feedback on how to get the confidence interval of the difference in slope.

You can get a CI by requesting it from the summary(..., ci = TRUE) or by default from parameterEstimates().

