Tere are some differences in articles and book chapters . One chapter suggests:
configural invaraince
metric/weak invariance: equal factor loadings as a precondition for comparing covariances between groups
scalar/strong invariance: plus equal intersepts of manifest indicators as a precondition for comparing latent means
strict factorial invariance: plus equal variances and covariances of latent variables
strict measurement error invariance/strict resiudal variance: plus equal residual variance

Can someone explain to me if the model five is necessary to compare variances between groups or not?

